        {
          "author": "Gregory Price (author)",
          "summary": "The author is addressing Lorenzo's concern about the testing mechanisms used in the patch, specifically selftests and their limitations. The author acknowledges that selftests are limited and create a maintenance burden, but explains that they have been exploring other testing mechanisms such as Usermode Linux (UML) and Linux Test Project to stub out reclaim calls and demonstrate basic correctness for the page allocator.\n\nThe author is addressing a concern about the testability of mm/ code, specifically providing statistics on how much of the codebase is currently testable and mentioning plans to make more extensive unit tests for certain parts of mm/. The author does not explicitly state that they will address any specific issues or concerns raised by Lorenzo, but instead seems to be sharing information about their testing infrastructure.",
          "sentiment": "neutral",
          "sentiment_signals": [
            "acknowledges limitations",
